<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Davos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Davos is a town in the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Graubünden</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, set in a high Alpine valley at about 1,560 metres. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-the-ten-jurisdictions">League of the Ten Jurisdictions</a> was formed there in 1436, and in the 19th century it became a health resort for tuberculosis patients, the setting of Thomas Mann's The Magic Mountain. Since 1971 it has hosted the annual meeting of the World Economic Forum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/davos.jpg" alt="Davos" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MadGeographer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:City_of_Davos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
